**What changed and why:**

| Concern | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| **Config** | Hardcoded at module top | `os.environ.get()` with safe defaults; `DB_PASS` defaults to empty string |
| **SQL injection** | `%`-formatting into SQL strings | `cur.execute("INSERT ... VALUES (?, ?)", (...))` — no string interpolation |
| **Structure** | One 90-line `proc_data()` | Six single-responsibility functions: `extract_log_entries`, `transform_errors`, `transform_api_metrics`, `load_to_db`, `generate_html_report`, `run_pipeline` |
| **Log parsing** | `line.split()` + fragile `in` checks | Three compiled regex patterns (`_RE_LOG`, `_RE_USER`, `_RE_API`) |
| **Types** | None | `TypedDict` for all record types, full signatures on every function |
| **Docstrings** | None | Every function has a docstring with params, returns, and type hints |
| **HTML escaping** | None | Error messages and endpoint names are HTML-escaped before insertion |

**HTML output is identical in substance** — error summary with counts, API latency table, active session count — plus a generation timestamp added for traceability.

